  "why_wrong": "B. Viral meningitis shows a lymphocytosis with normal glucose and mildly raised protein. C. TB meningitis shows lymphocytes, very high protein and low glucose with a subacute course. D. This is clearly abnormal. E. SAH shows red cells/xanthochromia, not this cellular pattern.",
  "pearl": "Bacterial CSF: neutrophils ↑, protein ↑, glucose ↓. Viral: lymphocytes, normal glucose.",
