  "correct_letter": "A",
  "correct_answer": "A. Stop warfarin, give IV vitamin K and prothrombin complex concentrate",
  "why_correct": "Major bleeding on warfarin is reversed by stopping warfarin, giving IV vitamin K, and giving prothrombin complex concentrate (PCC), which replaces the vitamin-K-dependent clotting factors faster and more completely than FFP. PCC is preferred over FFP for rapid reversal in life-threatening bleeding.",
  "why_wrong": "B. Observation alone is unsafe in major bleeding. C. FFP alone is slower/less complete and warfarin must stop. D. Protamine reverses heparin, not warfarin. E. Oral vitamin K alone is too slow for major bleeding.",
  "pearl": "Major warfarin bleed → stop warfarin + IV vitamin K + PCC (PCC over FFP).",
  "thinking": "Warfarin + major bleed + high INR ↓ rapid full reversal ↓ stop + IV vitamin K + PCC",
  "exam_trap": "Reaching for FFP or protamine — major warfarin bleeding needs PCC plus IV vitamin K, and protamine is for heparin.",
