  "why_wrong": "A. ATN from dehydration is possible but the temporal link to the ACE inhibitor and the vascular history point to RAS. B. A 40% rise is beyond the acceptable range and is not simply 'expected'. C. Post-streptococcal GN follows infection in younger patients. D. Minimal change disease causes nephrotic syndrome, not this picture.",
  "pearl": "Big creatinine rise after starting an ACE inhibitor in a vasculopath = suspect bilateral renal artery stenosis.",
