  "why_correct": "Fundal pressure is contraindicated in shoulder dystocia because it further impacts the shoulder and increases the risk of uterine rupture and fetal injury. The correct sequence uses McRoberts positioning and suprapubic (not fundal) pressure, with internal manoeuvres if needed and early senior help.",
  "why_wrong": "A. An episiotomy may help access for internal manoeuvres. C. McRoberts is the recommended first manoeuvre. D. Suprapubic pressure is correct; fundal pressure is not. E. Senior help should be summoned immediately.",
