  "correct_answer": "D. Start metformin, adding insulin if targets are still not met",
  "why_correct": "When diet and exercise fail to achieve glucose targets in gestational diabetes, metformin is typically started, with insulin added if targets remain unmet (insulin may be first-line if glucose is very high or there are complications). Tight control reduces fetal macrosomia and other complications.",
  "why_wrong": "A. Sulfonylureas are not first-line in GDM. B. SGLT2 inhibitors are not used in pregnancy. C. Untreated hyperglycaemia harms the fetus. E. Continuing diet alone when targets are missed is inadequate.",
  "pearl": "GDM not at target on diet → metformin, then add insulin if needed.",
  "thinking": "GDM + targets missed after diet/exercise ↓ escalate ↓ metformin (± insulin)",
  "exam_trap": "Leaving gestational diabetes on diet alone when targets are missed — pharmacological treatment protects the fetus.",
  "takeaway": "When diet fails in gestational diabetes, start metformin and add insulin if targets are still unmet.",
