  "correct_letter": "E",
  "correct_answer": "E. Regular exercise/physiotherapy and NSAIDs",
  "why_correct": "First-line management of ankylosing spondylitis is a regular exercise and physiotherapy programme combined with NSAIDs, which improve pain, stiffness and function. Anti-TNF biologics are used if symptoms persist despite NSAIDs; systemic steroids and conventional DMARDs are of limited benefit for the axial disease.",
  "why_wrong": "A. Long-term systemic steroids are not standard for axial AS. B. Bed rest worsens stiffness; exercise is key. C. Methotrexate helps peripheral, not axial, disease. D. Surgery is reserved for specific structural complications.",
